end note

note bottom of LLVM_VERSION
  The version check ran one native program,
  but it did not compile or test the GPU path.
  Its matching output resolves the version
  question, not the need for native linking
  or actual GPU compilation evidence.
end note

note bottom of LLVM_INTEGRATION
  The review records the earlier proposal,
  not the later grant to change source.
  Its installer skip leaves native compilation
  and static linking intact, so source wiring
  alone cannot qualify the prepared GPU path.
end note

note bottom of PREPARED_LOCAL
  All six static stages passed after toolchain
  recovery, but the first offline tree failed.
  Its registry miss identifies one unresolved
  package, not a complete cache inventory or
  proof that the prepared host graph works.
end note

note bottom of PREPARED_TESTS
  Pure fixtures check paired compiler binding,
  so a Cargo path cannot imply a usable pair.
  They also keep the static environment intact;
  passing them establishes helper behavior,
  not actual host toolchain coupling.
end note

note bottom of RUST_REQUEST
  The one scoped installation grant is spent,
  so the original request permits no repeat.
  A successful install cannot prove the feature
  trees, whose offline checks must retain the
  exact repository Cargo and rustc binding.
end note

note bottom of RUST_SOURCE
  Mocked checks verify the bounded install plan,
  without invoking Mise or installing tools.
  Their passing receipt remains source evidence,
  not the actual install or failed offline
  resolution, which have separate receipts.
end note

note bottom of CACHE_REQUEST
  The registry limit counts locked package
  versions, not metadata requests or byte volume.
  Index records may include other versions
  without granting upgrades or changing the
  frozen dependency selection.
end note

note bottom of CACHE_HELPER
  The fetch clones its environment for online use,
  so shared checks retain offline configuration.
  Stable inputs and fetch success permit offline
  feature trees, not native linking or proof of
  GPU runtime qualification.
end note

note bottom of CACHE_RECHECK
  Each offline tree passed its feature checks,
  so resolved feature text is now actual evidence.
  Resolved features do not establish compiled
  host dependency sharing, native linking or
  GPU runtime qualification.
end note

